**Goal Model – Multi‑Robot Resource Delivery**

| Goal ID | Goal Title                     | Text                                                                                                           | Runtime Annotation | Goal Type | Relation |
|---------|--------------------------------|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|---------------------|-----------|----------|
| G1      | Complete Resource Delivery     | Ensure all requested resources are collected from storages and delivered to the requesting agent at the specified location. | –                   | Achieve   | –        |
| G2      | Perform Collection Phase       | Execute the collection of resources from storage locations.                                                    | ;                   | Perform   | G1       |
| G2.1    | Navigate to Storage           | Move robot to the storage location where resources are found.                                                   | –                   | Perform   | G2       |
| G2.2    | Request Resources              | Send message specifying requested resources to storage.                                                         | –                   | Perform   | G2       |
| G2.3    | Wait for Retrieval             | Wait until storage confirms resources retrieved.                                                               | –                   | Perform   | G2       |
| G2.4    | Check Battery Low in Collection | If battery <10 % → go to recharge and assign mission to another robot; otherwise continue collection.           | FALLBACK(G2.4.1,G2.4.2) | Perform | G2       |
| G2.4.1  | Handle Low Battery in Collection | Go to recharging station and assign mission to another robot.                                                 | ;                   | Perform   | G2.4     |
| G2.4.2  | Continue Collection             | Continue collection after battery check.                                                                        | –                   | Perform   | G2.4     |
| G3      | Perform Delivery Phase         | Execute delivery of collected resources to destination.                                                       | ;                   | Perform   | G1       |
| G3.1    | Transport Resources to Destination | Move resources from storage to specified location.                                                             | –                   | Perform   | G3       |
| G3.2    | Check Battery Low in Delivery | If battery <30 % → return resource to checkpoint and assign remaining task to another robot; otherwise continue delivery. | FALLBACK(G3.2.1,G3.2.2) | Perform | G3       |
| G3.2.1  | Handle Low Battery in Delivery | Return resource to checkpoint and assign remaining task to another robot.                                    | ;                   | Perform   | G3.2     |
| G3.2.2  | Continue Delivery               | Continue delivering remaining resources.                                                                       | –                   | Perform   | G3.2     |
| G3.2.1.1 | Return Resource to Checkpoint | Attempt to return resource to checkpoint; if fails, alert and report.                                         | FALLBACK(AT7,AT9)  | Perform   | G3.2.1   |
| G3.2.1.2 | Assign Remaining Task to Another Robot | Transfer remaining task to another robot after low battery.                                                   | –                   | Perform   | G3.2.1   |
| G7      | Parallelize Collect‑Deliver Tasks | Assign multiple robots to parallel collect‑deliver tasks when multiple items are required.                    | #                   | Perform   | G1       |

---

### Task Model

| Task ID | Task Title                     | Text                                                                                                 | Relation | Location                | Number of Robots |
|---------|---------------------------------|--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|----------|------------------------|-------------------|
| AT1     | Navigate to Storage             | Move robot to the storage location where resources are found.                                         | AND      | Storage_Location       | 1                 |
| AT2     | Send Request Message            | Send message specifying requested resources to storage.                                               | AND      | Storage_Location       | 1                 |
| AT3     | Wait for Resource Retrieval    | Wait until storage confirms resources retrieved.                                                      | AND      | Storage_Location       | 1                 |
| AT4     | Go to Recharging Station        | Move robot to recharging station due to low battery.                                                  | AND      | Recharging_Station      | 1                 |
| AT5     | Assign Mission to Another Robot | Transfer mission assignment to another robot.                                                          | AND      | Recharging_Station      | 1                 |
| AT6     | Transport Resources to Destination | Move resources from storage to specified location.                                                     | AND      | Delivery_Destination   | 1                 |
| AT7     | Return Resource to Checkpoint  | Return resource to checkpoint due to low battery.                                                      | AND      | Checkpoint             | 1                 |
| AT8     | Continue Delivery               | Continue delivering remaining resources.                                                               | AND      | Delivery_Destination   | 1                 |
| AT9     | Alert and Report to Sector Manager | Trigger alert and send report due to failure to return resource.                                      | AND      | Sector_Manager         | 1                 |
| AT10    | Assign Remaining Task to Another Robot | Transfer remaining task to another robot after low battery.                                            | AND      | Checkpoint             | 1                 |
| AT11    | Parallel Collect‑Deliver Tasks  | Assign multiple robots to parallel collect‑deliver tasks.                                             | AND      | Storage_Location, Delivery_Destination | [1,n] |

---

### Logical Relationships

* **G1** is the root goal and decomposes into **G2**, **G3**, and **G7** (AND).  
* **G2** decomposes sequentially into **G2.1 → G2.2 → G2.3 → G2.4** (AND).  
* **G2.4** is a fallback between **G2.4.1** (handle low battery) and **G2.4.2** (continue collection).  
* **G3** decomposes sequentially into **G3.1 → G3.2** (AND).  
* **G3.2** is a fallback between **G3.2.1** (handle low battery) and **G3.2.2** (continue delivery).  
* **G3.2.1** decomposes into **AT7** and **AT10** (AND).  
* **G3.2.1.1** is a fallback between **AT7** (return to checkpoint) and **AT9** (alert/report).  
* **G7** runs in parallel (#) and decomposes into **AT11** (parallel collect‑deliver tasks).  

This goal–task model captures the mission’s operational flow, battery‑aware contingencies, and the possibility of parallel execution when multiple items are requested.
